factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The reel_script and slides_spec say the police are "checking" the station as a whole, but the article gives no detail beyond checks on passengers' belongings and bags, so this is a mild embellishment — though it stays within the article's scope.
  The caption says the measure was taken "to prevent drug trafficking and criminal activity" and that "கஞ்சா போதைப்பொருள் கடத்தப்படுகிறதா என்று ஆய்வு செய்யப்பட்டது" is fine, but the caption's first line says the police were conducting checks "in the Deepavali crowd" (தீபாவளி கூட்டத்தில்), which is a loose rendering of the article's point about using the crowd, not a stated location detail.
  The slides_spec says the inspector's team is doing "திருட்டைத் தடுக்கவும் கண்காணிப்பு" (surveillance to prevent theft), which the article does not state; the article only asks passengers to keep belongings safe.
  The caption's last paragraph says the police asked passengers to keep belongings safe, which is accurate, but the reel_script says the police "கேட்டுக்கொண்டனர்" in a way that is grammatically acceptable; no real factual error here, so this is noted only for completeness.
